<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The launch window's icon: the unlit ground and nothing on it.

     This is not an oversight and it is not a placeholder. Android 12 and
     later draw a splash on every cold start whether an app asks for one or
     not, from the launching activity's theme, in the system process, before
     the app exists — and if no icon is named the platform falls back to the
     launcher icon on a plate, which is the one thing A28 set out to avoid.
     Naming an empty vector is the only way to say "the ground, please, and
     leave the mark to us".

     Why to us: the mark is `design/LaunchMark.kt` now, on the app's first
     frame, because the animated version of it in the launch theme did not
     play on the owner's phone and a system-drawn window is not something
     this app can see, test or fix. The drawable itself was checked and was
     never the problem.

     The viewport matches `splash_wave.xml` so the two are interchangeable in
     the theme, which matters the one time it is worth being able to swap
     them back. -->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <path android:pathData="M0,0 Z" android:fillColor="#00000000" />
</vector>
